PURPOSE Run declared paper-method case/variant combinations with traceable outputs.
INPUT case manifest, transfer/sharing variants, resource and output configuration
OUTPUT per-case status, validated routes and metric tables
REFERENCES Program; Generating_TS_RS_results

PROCEDURE RunBatch(manifest,configuration)
    FOR each declared case and variant
        resolve required coordinate/window/flag/schedule files from the manifest
        input := LoadCase(case.directory,case.selection,configuration)
        effectiveConfig := configuration with the declared transfer/sharing and
            operational variant; LoadCase applies these explicit overrides
        allocate a unique case/variant output directory
        record input fingerprints, paper-method version and effective configuration
        result := RunSplitDecomposition(case.directory,effectiveConfig)
        IF result.bestFeasiblePlan exists
            validate and export plan, costs, service metrics and search history
        ELSE
            export status and unresolved work without reading unavailable values
        IF variant requests periodic updates and result.bestFeasiblePlan exists
            RunDynamicEpochs(result.bestFeasiblePlan,input.arrivals,
                             configuration.epochs,input,configuration)
        preserve all solver/limit/stop statuses in the per-case record
    return per-case result table

PROCEDURE RunTransferSharingVariants(case)
    FOR each explicitly listed permission combination
        clone input records; set the actual transfer/sharing eligibility flags
        route to the selected static or periodic paper-method procedure
        report effective inputs, validated outputs and metrics
    compare results only under matching cost, time-grid and demand conventions

PROCEDURE RunInitializationProbe(case)
    input := LoadCase(case.directory,case.selection,case.configuration)
    network := BuildNetwork(input,input.configuration)
    pool,initialSolutions := CreateSeedPool(network,input)
    return route coefficients, physical/unserved labels and seed statuses

ASSUMPTIONS
    Each manifest entry identifies its inputs, limits and output location.
    Transfer/sharing variants change model eligibility as well as report labels.
    The paper capacity equation counts package units. Exclusive service with
    full-capacity load is a separate scenario option.
